  "$comment": [
    "SHARED, CANONICAL parity fixture for spec 12 (Application Form Serving Redesign), task 5.3.",
    "It pins the frontend in-browser preview filter (buildPreviewConfig, applicationPreviewFilter.ts)",
    "to the SAM server filter authority (MembershipService.get_public_field_config) so retiring the",
    "server preview endpoint (task 5.2) can never let the two silently drift (R3.2 / R9.1 / R9.2).",
    "",
    "ONE file is canonical: sam/tests/fixtures/application_form_filter_parity.json. The frontend test",
    "root carries a byte-identical vendored copy at",
    "frontend/src/components/TenantAdmin/MembersConfig/__tests__/fixtures/application_form_filter_parity.json;",
    "a guard test on EACH plane asserts the two copies are byte-for-byte identical, so an edit to one",
    "that is not mirrored to the other fails loudly. Both planes feed `input` to their REAL filter,",
    "normalize the output to the plane-neutral `expected` shape, and assert equality against the SAME",
    "`expected` block below.",
    "",
    "How each plane consumes `input`:",
    " - FRONTEND: buildPreviewConfig takes an ALREADY-RESOLVED FieldConfig + the working overlay. The",
    "   frontend adapter builds FieldConfig.fields straight from `input.resolved_fields` and applies no",
    "   overlay (the application attributes are already resolved onto each field here).",
    " - SAM: get_public_field_config resolves a TenantOverlay over the platform fixed base. The SAM",
    "   adapter rebuilds that overlay from `input.resolved_fields`: every field whose `group` is",
    "   `overlay` becomes a tenant-added OverlayField; the one `membership.membership_type` field is a",
    "   fixed-field OVERRIDE carrying only the application attributes (its label/type/order/group come",
    "   from the platform registry and are mirrored in `input.resolved_fields` + `expected` so the two",
    "   planes agree).",
    "",
    "Shape notes:",
    " - `input.resolved_fields` use the bare `key` + storage `group` server shape (R2.3).",
    " - membership-type catalog labels use EQUAL nl/en text so the two planes' label resolution agree",
    "   without weakening any assertion (the frontend catalog resolver collapses to one string).",
    " - `expected.fields` is the canonical applicant-facing SELECTION both filters must produce, in",
    "   resolver order (group, order, key). `options` is always present (null for a non-choice field)",
    "   so the two normalized shapes compare like-for-like."
  ],
